<article class="env-lemma" id="0GDG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GDG">Lemma <span data-tag="0GDG">88.23.7</span>.</a> In the situation above. If $f$ is (quasi-)separated, then $f_{/T}$ is too. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      (Separation conditions on morphisms of formal algebraic spaces are discussed in Formal Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/0ARM" data-tag="0ARM">87.30</a>.) We have to show that if $\Delta _ f$ is quasi-compact, resp. a closed immersion, then the same is true for $\Delta _{f_{/T}}$. This follows from the discussion in Remark <a href="/tag/0GDF" data-tag="0GDF">88.23.6</a> and Lemmas <a href="/tag/0GDE" data-tag="0GDE">88.23.5</a> and <a href="/tag/0GDC" data-tag="0GDC">88.23.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>